                <head>363. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>On Sunday, November 13, Secretary of State Dulles held a meeting on disarmament with his senior staff at 9
                    a.m. At 10, he and Foreign Minister Molotov met at his office in the Palais des Nations to consider
                    United Nations membership, trade controls on China, the tanker <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Tuapse</hi>, the future work of the conference, and the
                    Middle East. Following the meeting with Molotov, Dulles and
                        Merchant had lunch with Macmillan. In the evening, the Secretary and his
                    principal advisers discussed East-West contacts, and at 6:50 Dulles reviewed the disarmament question with
                        Stassen. (Department of State,
                    Conference Files: Lot 60 D 627, CF 584)</p>
                <p>A record of the meeting with Molotov
                    follows. A brief memorandum of the lunch with Macmillan is <hi rendition="#italic">ibid</hi>. No records have
                    been found for the other meetings in Department of State files.</p>
            </div>
